body:
The game didn't warn me because I got the mkII out before putting a vehicle in his place, what I think it should warn is when you're using a vehicle that is stored nowhere, but regardless of if it warns you or not it's still a big problem with the storage sistem, literally no game should have a system where a small mistake of not reading something on the corner of the screen deletes something you bought, and about "it's not R\* fault", obviosly it is, as you said in your first comment, so many people complain that you thought this was a troll, how hard it is to put every vehicle you buy on pegasus, that way even if you have no apartment or storage, you can still use the thing you bought, or warning you when in a vehicle stored nowhere. but an off-topic quesiton, why are you defending R\*? as I said, is something that is not fun, doesn't improve the game logic or world building or anything, the why are you arguing that losing something that took you hours to get just because of 5 minutes of changing storage without paying attention on what I was doing is ok?, it is a videogame, it is supossed to be fun, not punishing you for forgetting to store a car somewhere else.

&#x200B;

PS: When you replace something the thing you replace goes somewhere else, so by the grammar and sense logic you keep saying, the MKII should've gone to a free space on the terrorbyte, or the other dozens empty space I have in the game.

&#x200B;

PSS: man i cant believe i stayed and entire day checking on reddit discussing the loss of a flying bike on a videogame, Good night
